-- end (drizzle-kit does not emit triggers; the 0057/0063 pattern).
--
-- Rule R1, enforced here so no code path can break it: the stock switch is ON only while
-- orders_apply_enabled is ON (CHECK), and turning orders_apply_enabled OFF turns the stock switch OFF in
-- the same row write (BEFORE UPDATE trigger, only on the ON -> OFF transition, so an attempt to turn
-- stock ON while orders are OFF still fails on the CHECK instead of being silently ignored).
--
-- Backward compatibility with the previous release (CLAUDE.md expand/contract): additive only. The new
-- table and the three new columns are never read by the previous release; the new column defaults to
-- false so its inserts keep working. Its "Hentikan penerapan pesanan" (orders_apply_enabled = false)
-- still works and, through the trigger, also turns stock sync off, so R1 holds after a rollback too. The
-- cursor CHECK becomes a superset (dropped and re-added in this one transaction, the 0040 pattern); the
-- previous release never writes `products`. No reference data (hold reasons are CHECK values).
-- Locks: short ones on two small tables; lock_timeout fails fast (and rolls back) instead of queueing.

SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';--> statement-breakpoint
